oves position without weakening White.\n\nReason:  \nc2-c4 is the most constructive move — it stakes a claim in the center, enables faster development of minor pieces, and avoids passive play. Other moves are either too slow (like rook shuffling) or less impactful (h3-h4). This move maximizes long-term winning chances by improving piece activity.\n\nAnswer: P: c2-c4"}
